# Run ROAM on an Example Subject
In this file, we provide a tutorial to run ROAM on an example subject [privacy-friendly-weather#61](https://github.com/SecUSo/privacy-friendly-weather/issues/61). Before continue to the next steps, please make sure your local machine satisified the hardware requirements and software requirements in the "REQUIREMENTS.md" file.

### Run ROAM
To run ROAM on the demo example, execute the following command in the bash interface within the docker container if you are using docker to setup the environment. If you are not using docker, execute the command in the "ReproductionTool" directory. For more details of the input arguments, please refer to section "Input Arguments" in README.md file.
```bash
# Estimated Time: 3m10s
python3 -u tool_main.py \
  --appId saner2022-23 \
  --apkPath ./test_input/app.apk \
  --outputDir ./output \
  --s2rsPath ./test_input/s2r_groundtruth.json \
  --crashMsgPath ./test_input/errormsg.txt \
  --utgPath ./test_input/gui_model \
  --androidVersion "Android 7" \
  -createNewEmulator
```
When you see "TOOL Ended. Result: Success" generated in the command line, the tool finished running. You will find the output generated in the specified output folder "./ReproductionTool/output". For explanation of the output files, please refer to Section "Output Structure" in README.md.</output>
